- With the partitioned flag: Morsel.OutputString() includes 'Partitioned' as a bare attribute.
- SameSite is correctly capitalized (e.g., 'SameSite=None').
- Secure and HttpOnly continue to emit as flags when set.

Pitfalls and environment quirks
- Cythonized methods and runtime monkey patching:
  - In environments where Falcon uses cythonized implementations (cyfunction) for Response methods, changing the Python source signature does not update the compiled method.
  - A runtime wrapper is required to accept new kwargs; ensure it is applied early enough in the import sequence. Patching in falcon/__init__.py proved reliable in our tests; relying on util/__init__.py alone did not always apply early enough without explicitly reloading the module.
- Morsel reserved attributes:
  - When backporting 'partitioned' into Morsel._reserved, the attribute key may exist on the Morsel with an empty value by default. Do not assert on absence solely via key presence; check value truthiness or the absence of the 'Partitioned' directive in Set-Cookie headers.
